  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so the primary uncertainty is the performance floor: what can a simple single-modality model achieve? config_014 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest, most interpretable RNA baseline available. It establishes a clean reference point with minimal confounding (no image modality, no learned encoder, no aggregation/fusion), so any future improvement can be attributed to specific design choices (better RNA encoder, adding image modality, multiprofile, aggregation, fusion). Starting from this floor is the most information-efficient first step: it calibrates expectations, confirms the pipeline works, and provides the anchor against which all subsequent multimodal and multiprofile experiments will be judged. Under a limited budget, a clean baseline is more valuable than an early gamble on a complex configuration whose gains cannot yet be decomposed."
}

